{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"PHASE 1 RCA (2026-08-15)\n\nProven mechanism: `.github/workflows/_build-and-test.yml` sends the same `not integration and not external` default selection through Ubuntu 3.11/3.12/3.13 and macOS 3.13. Nineteen audited nodes inspect only immutable repository text/AST, so their assertions are redundantly executed four times even though OS/Python cannot change their input or expected result. The exact nodes are pinned in this ticket.\n\nDiscriminating evidence: latest successful Gerrit Verify run 31892203411 took 31m59s; macOS default was 1,545.29s and integration 155.01s, with no individual macOS test over 30s. The exact 19-node set passed locally under `-n 3` in 8.28s. Mixed-module inspection rejected whole-file routing: the same files contain runtime/subprocess contracts that can expose macOS-only defects. Workflow inspection rejected a new Ubuntu shard: it would repeat checkout/install/collection/session setup and consume another runner. Keeping the nodes in the already-running Ubuntu 3.13 cell adds zero runner or fixture cost.\n\nAlternatives ruled out: blanket macOS reduction violates the platform-compatibility contract and closed ticket ropeable-hydrated-siskin; extra sharding violates coercive-paediatric-bug and the operator constraint. Five active OSS projects (pytest, pip, Pydantic, Click, uv) retain behavioral suites on macOS while routing static/lint policy to Linux, so the narrow singleton route meets the standing consensus bar.\n\nDefect legitimacy: defect against the explicit no-redundant-runner-use requirement, limited to invariant policy duplication. General macOS behavioral duplication is intended coverage and remains unchanged. Expected benefit is modest: about 8 seconds macOS / 24.84 aggregate runner-seconds in the measured local environment, not a standalone fix for a 32-minute run. Plan review PASS; Phase 2 may begin."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786815092028844001,"uuid":"3f71dfbd-8b6c-46a4-98b4-413f46e023a7"}